Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||08-03-2001||11:24 AM||||I don't like to show the stereotype image of a Fiero, but I was digging through my volumes of photos taken looking for Fiero stuff. I decided that this was worth posting just for the humor (sadness?) of it.  This WAS an '86 SE V6 we purchased for $20 (delivered).  I don't really know the story of what actually happened to the car, but It was TOAST!  I did use one piece of lower trim on the right side of the car for my '87 GT... which alone made up for the cost of the car. Just thought I'd share some pics with you!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierofire1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierofire3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierofire2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||10
