Z||000019||MinnGreenGT||08-06-2001||10:14 AM||||As for paying for the car... my brother-in-law worked for the towing company at the time, and we gave him $20 to drop it off at our house.<P><BR>As for my GreenGT... the wheels are the stock '87's... had Precision Wheel Service here in Bloomington, MN totally refinish them.  They sandblast the whole wheel, polish the edge (&clearcoat) and powdercoated the center using "honeywheat" (ford gold color).  They are a little lighter in gold color than the stock '88s and match the green very nicely.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
